('recYEgqSt1V6onP2X', '2026-01-15', NULL, 'SVM', 8, 45, NULL, 'January 15, 2026 – Progress Update Project: Coresite SV9 Phase 3 Percentage of Completion: 100%   Scope of Works Completed: Completed modeling of the wire gutter (gutter box), including dimensions and supports, based on details provided today. Finalized all outstanding concerns, sheets, and the Revit model. Successfully aligned the exported NWC file with the General Contractor’s Federated Navisworks model. Notes: Multiple alignment methods were attempted; however, the original RVT file did not display correctly in the federated Navisworks model. As a last-resort solution, following the given instruction, the method below was used. a. Opened SV9-P3_ARCH from ACC, deleted all elements, and saved it as a new file to serve as an alignment template for future work. b. Copied and pasted all elements from my RVT file into the Level 2 Floor Plan of the newly created template. c. Exported the 3D view to an NWC file using Shared Coordinates (Project Internal did not align) and appended it to the original Federated Navisworks model from ACC.   Deliverables (Uploaded to ACC): NWC file (Shared Coordinates) Revit model PDF sheets', 'NO', NULL, '2026-01-16', 'Approved', '2026-01-15', 'N'),
