('recblQXiCWdDfvSZH', '2025-12-10', NULL, 'Ikaika', 8, 0, NULL, 'December 10, 2025 CORESITE SV9 Phase 3 General Notes Review: Install 6” conduit below grade with minimum 3 conduit containing 1 ¼” innerduct and 3 conduits containing 2” innerduct Provide Fire-rated Plywood on all walls of each POE. See Archi. Roof Provision Rigid Steel Conduit shall have Pull string, cap and seal Single mode fiber optic cable installed in conduit is non armored Conduit runs more than 100’ should have pull box All conduit ends should have bushing Cable Tray should be supported by cantilever brackets, Unistrut trapeze, & individual rod suspension brackets Trays and wireways shall be supported on 5’ centers and supports must be within 2’ of any fitting For conduits with internal diameter <2” Inside radius is 6X the inside diameter if EMT 10X if PVC For conduits with internal diameter >2” Inside radius is 10X the inside diameter Pull boxes shall not be used for splicing cable or used in lieu of a conduit bend Bond SRG with #10 Bare copper ground conductor with maximum every 60’ Typical 4” conduit innerduct – (3) 1.25” HDPE - Split Duct Plug and Inside vault leave 24”( diff between 4” and 1.25”) and 10ft pull tape Leave 1’ slack in Cable Tray & Cat 6 UTP cables terminated with 8P/8C Connectors All conduit fittings shall be bonded e.g. bushing LF Pull box sizing chart & pathway labeling convention @ Page 8', 'NO', NULL, '2025-12-10', 'Approved', '2025-12-10', 'N'),
